<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Castillo de San Marcos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1672">1672</a>–<a href="/years/1695">1695</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Castillo de San Marcos is a Spanish masonry fort at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/st-augustine-florida">St. Augustine, Florida</a>, built between 1672 and 1695 from coquina, a local shell stone. It replaced a series of wooden forts and withstood English sieges in 1702 and 1740, which burned the town but never took the fort. The oldest masonry fort in the continental <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, it is now a national monument.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/castillo-de-san-marcos.jpg" alt="Castillo de San Marcos" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Schwerdf · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aerial_view_of_the_Castillo_de_San_Marcos,_St._Augustine,_FL_2025-05-20.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
